# use case: a developer hardens the application and tests it.
title The rules say what the application accepts, an expect line next to each says what it must refuse and let through, and CI tests every one before a deploy
row  code:box "A new endpoint" "or a new parameter" | rule:warnbox "A rule and its examples" "query, allow, restrict, expect" | ci:okbox "request-shield test in CI" "JUnit, exit 1 on a failure"
row  monitor:warnbox "Deployed, watched" "monitor: logs, refuses nobody" | enforce:okbox "Enforced" "remove the word monitor"
arrow code -> rule
arrow rule -> ci go
arrow ci -> monitor "all pass"
arrow monitor -> enforce "no false hits" go
note The application still checks its input; the shield refuses the junk before the framework starts.
